From cf48f0a7b73d96bc999a9590203c56e3ad5fbfc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orlfman <25542856+orlfman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:40:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] linux: support AMD CPU package power and harden RAPL
 sampling

The package power meter now accepts any readable RAPL package counter,
including AMD's, and shows watts alone when no long-term limit (PL1)
is reported; bar fill and graph use the limit when there is one. The
Setup names are vendor-neutral.

Packages are grouped by name across the intel-rapl (MSR) and
intel-rapl-mmio interfaces and counted once, with MSR preferred and
MMIO as the fallback for energy and for the limit. Each zone is read
through one opened directory: its name is rechecked (a reused path
triggers rediscovery), and its identity, counter and wrap range come
from the same directory, so a replaced counter starts a new baseline
instead of looking like a wrap.

The meter takes its timestamp from linux/MeterClock.h: monotonicMs
while it advances, and the clock once per header pass while the
process list is paused (Z), so package watts keep updating.

Co-Authored-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6.2 Astra) <noreply@openai.com>
